input.message:
Fix round 2. I reviewed your round-1 fix (commit 8bfd69a) myself before sending it to review, and found two things to correct — plus the mandated smoke test still needs to actually run to completion.

## 1. The split into `biome lint` + `biome format --write` wasn't necessary — revert to one `biome check --write` command

I tested this myself, empirically, before writing this message: `--config-path` does NOT fix the nested-root-config error (confirmed — still fails identically even with `--config-path=frontend`). So your move away from a plain `biome check` command was right. But I also tested this, from cwd=`frontend`:

```bash
cd frontend && node_modules/.bin/biome check --write src/App.tsx
```

This runs cleanly — no nested-root error, exit 0. So the fix only needed the `cd` + path-remapping you already built; splitting into two separate commands (`lint` then `format --write`) was an extra, unrequested change. It also has a real side effect I want you to avoid: splitting drops the import-organizer assist step that `biome check` includes (`biome lint` and `biome format` each skip it). Confirmed concretely — running `biome check --write src/App.tsx` from `frontend/` actually fixed a real, previously-unaddressed finding:

```diff
-import { useState, useEffect, useCallback, useRef, useMemo } from "react";
+import { useCallback, useEffect, useMemo, useRef, useState } from "react";
```

(I reverted this test edit myself — `git status` is clean again — so you'll see it happen fresh when you run it for real.)

This also matches the plan's Global Constraint text exactly ("lint-staged's frontend entry becomes `biome check --write` (format + lint + import sort)") — a single command, not two. Please update `.lintstagedrc.mjs` so the frontend entry returns ONE command string using `biome check --write`, keeping your existing path-remapping logic (the regex extracting the path relative to `frontend/` is good — keep it), e.g.:

```js
export default {
  'frontend/src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}': (files) => {
    const relativePaths = files
      .map((file) => {
        const match = file.match(/frontend\/(.+)$/);
        return match ? match[1] : file.replace(/^frontend\//, '');
      })
      .join(' ');
    return `cd frontend && node_modules/.bin/biome check --write ${relativePaths}`;
  },
  'backend/*.py': [
    'backend/.venv/bin/ruff format',
    'backend/.venv/bin/ty check',
  ],
};
```

(You can adjust the exact regex/style if yours differs — the point is one command, `biome check --write`, not two.)

Also update the root `format` npm script in `package.json` to use `biome check --write` instead of `biome format --write`, for the same reason (it currently only formats — it should also catch lint/import-sort issues, matching what the hook now does). Keep it scoped to `src` the same way it already is (`cd frontend && node_modules/.bin/biome check --write src`).

## 2. Actually run the full smoke test this time

Your report said validation "hasn't been fully validated under all conditions in this session due to context limits." That's the one thing this fix round exists to prove — it can't be skipped. After making the change above, run the real 4-step test from my previous message in full:

1. Trivial single-quote edit to `frontend/src/App.tsx` (e.g. `const API_URL = "/api";` → single quotes), `git add`, `git commit -m "test: verify biome pre-commit hook (auto-fix)"`. Expect: commit succeeds, `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD -- frontend/src/App.tsx` shows NO diff.
2. `git reset --soft HEAD~1 && git restore --staged frontend/src/App.tsx && git checkout -- frontend/src/App.tsx`.
3. Remove `vowels.has` from the dependency array (`}, [phase, consonantPositions, vowels.has]);` → `}, [phase, consonantPositions]);`), `git add`, attempt `git commit -m "test: verify biome pre-commit hook (blocking)"`. Expect: commit FAILS, output specifically names `useExhaustiveDependencies`.
4. `git checkout -- frontend/src/App.tsx`. Confirm `git status --porcelain` empty and `git log -1 --oneline` shows your fix commit as HEAD.

Report the exact output of all four steps — don't summarize, paste the real terminal output into your report (append a "Fix round 2" section to the existing report file: /Users/rod/build/missing-vowels/.claude/worktrees/biome-migration/.superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-biome-migration/task-3-report.md).

Then reply with ONLY:
- Status: DONE, DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, NEEDS_CONTEXT, or BLOCKED
- The fix commit hash
- Confirmation both real smoke tests passed exactly as described (not partially, not "should work")
- Any concerns

